WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.999 --> 00:00:04.001
AudioSilo on an iPad. Home opens on the book I’m in the middle of.

2
00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:06.985
Tap to pick up where I left off.

3
00:00:06.985 --> 00:00:08.974
The player docks at the bottom. Tap it for the full player.

4
00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:12.376
This chapter in bars, the whole book underneath, and who’s who beside it.

5
00:00:12.376 --> 00:00:16.608
Jump ahead, with a way back for ten seconds.

6
00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:24.048
Speed and sleep are one tap away.

7
00:00:24.048 --> 00:00:25.251
Who’s who follows along as I listen.

8
00:00:25.251 --> 00:00:30.055
Reach a new chapter and the people I’ve just met appear.

9
00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:36.700
Everyone later in the book stays hidden until I get there.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:44.141
Up next is my queue, with the rest of the series suggested underneath.

11
00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:50.526
Series are shelves, in reading order.

12
00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.681
Books I don’t own yet stand on the shelf as ghost spines.

13
00:00:56.681 --> 00:01:03.870
The book page carries community recaps, cut off at my chapter.

14
00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:08.932
My listening: the week, the streak, and the days I listened.

15
00:01:08.932 --> 00:01:11.534
When I listen, and who I listen to.

16
00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:16.651
The Journal keeps my bookmarks and notes, with where they are in the book.

17
00:01:16.651 --> 00:01:25.184
My year in listening, as a story.

18
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:29.349
The same app runs on the web, iPhone and iPad.
